      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To determine the volume of the inscribed sphere, we start by understanding the relationship between the sphere and the cube. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Given that the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches. Therefore, the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of the diameter:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\( r = 3 \\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\( 3^3 \\):\n\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nSo the volume becomes:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27\n\\]\n\nSimplifying the expression:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4 \\times 27}{3} \\pi = \\frac{108}{3} \\pi = 36 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36\\pi}\n\\] cubic inches.",
