      "text": "To determine the volume of the inscribed sphere, we first need to identify the radius of the sphere. Since the sphere is inscribed in the cube, the diameter of the sphere is equal to the edge length of the cube. Given that the edge length of the cube is 6 inches, the diameter of the sphere is also 6 inches. Therefore, the radius \\( r \\) of the sphere is half of the diameter, which is:\n\n\\[\nr = \\frac{6}{2} = 3 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\n\nThe formula for the volume \\( V \\) of a sphere is given by:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi r^3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the radius \\( r = 3 \\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi (3)^3\n\\]\n\nCalculating \\( 3^3 \\):\n\n\\[\n3^3 = 27\n\\]\n\nSo the volume becomes:\n\n\\[\nV = \\frac{4}{3} \\pi \\times 27 = \\frac{4 \\times 27 \\pi}{3} = \\frac{108 \\pi}{3} = 36 \\pi\n\\]\n\nThus, the volume of the inscribed sphere is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{36\\pi}\n\\]",
